WI-540: rework REVIEW-A — route-keyed store, template-fed governing hash, wired OPENAI/OPENCODE telemetry

Addresses the round-002 verdict (CHANGES-REQUESTED, findings=6) on bb31d58.
Session 003 died mid-rework on a provider usage limit; this session reconciled
its residue, completed the missing regression pins, and re-verified.

MAJOR 1 — the store is keyed by (family, route_id), not family alone: the
route id is hashed into the filename and verified verbatim after parsing;
load_family enumerates one family for the dispatcher keep-warm; a launch with
no route id is a no-op. A stored OPENAI-A session can no longer be resumed for
OPENAI-B (driven).

MAJOR 2 — the governing hash now folds in the actually loaded adjudicate-*
prompts: map_preflight returns the real path per loaded prompt (override-
aware), resolve_session_setup carries the four brief paths on the LoopContext,
and route_session hands them to adjudicator_launch; editing a judging
instruction drains and retires the session at the next clear point (driven at
the hash, the preflight wiring, and the launch).

MAJOR 3 — OPENAI/OPENCODE telemetry is wired: context_telemetry joins the
emitted thread/session id to the exact Codex rollout under the launch
CODEX_HOME (never --last or the ambient home) or reads the opencode stream;
bookkeeping persists the captured id so later launches resume; session_meta
merges the retained columns over the WI-535 tuple blank by blank (driven for
both families).

MINORs — IF-174 Rationale states the standing reason only; IF-174 Data is a
typed pointer to the owner contract (99 chars, under the 160 ceiling);
adjudicator_session.py carries the Contracts: IF-174 header and contract body.

Adjacent: dispatch keep-warm enumerates per-route records; LLR-163/TC-157/IF-064
re-pointed at the adapter seam; module-size ratchet re-stamped DOWN (agent_loop
2640->2622, agent_common 1300->1299) with reasons; the complexity baseline
route_session entry dropped back under the floor; smoke membership 1478 vs the
1482 ceiling, no re-stamp owed.

Commit bar: smoke 1448 passed / 30 skipped (posix-shell gate), 25.8s vs 60s
budget within; check_docs OK (0 broken); gen_open_items --check: 0 pending
rows, nothing contradicts (the html freshness regen is the trunk lane's step).

